# cp elasticsearch.env.example elasticsearch.env and fill it in. elasticsearch.env is gitignored.
#
#   ssh -J supervisor@<hypervisor> supervisor@10.42.0.22 \
#     'sudo cat /etc/homelab/elasticsearch_app_password'
#
# The `app` account, not `elastic` — the superuser stays break-glass. Its role is confined to
# `elasticsearch_index_pattern` in the homelab inventory, which has to cover the index the
# article service actually writes. That index is `articles`, a const in
# ElasticsearchIndexerHostedService.cs, so the pattern must be `articles*` and not the
# default `app-*`; otherwise every index call comes back 403 and the ES indexer never commits
# an offset.
ELASTIC_PASSWORD=
